  "term": "3,4-dihydroxyphenylalanine",
  "definition": "3,4-dihydroxyphenylalanine, also called DOPA, is a precursor chemical to dopamine. In this honey bee study, higher dietary tyrosine or royal jelly was linked with higher DOPA levels in the hemolymph and higher dopamine levels in venom.",
