      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports that 3,4-dihydroxyphenylalanine is abbreviated DOPA and that it was measured as a dopamine precursor in honey bee hemolymph, but it does not explicitly establish the general definitional claim that it is “a precursor chemical to dopamine.”",
        "The honey bee finding about tyrosine or royal jelly increasing DOPA in hemolymph and dopamine in venom is supported, but the definition blends that study result with a broader biochemical definition in a way that is not fully supported by the packet."
